                <pb facs="1018" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg922"/>

                <head>No. 584.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-06"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 6,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Official Gazette publishes telegram from captain-general of Cuba, reporting
                    capture of Virginius six miles from Jamaica, after a chase, by Spanish steamer
                    Tornado. In compliance with my suggestion, instructions sent to captain-general
                    to await orders from this government before indicting penalties on passengers or
                    crew.</p>
                <closer><signed>SICKLES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
